/*!
@defgroup emu
@ingroup mod_system ECC Management Unit (EMU)
@brief ECC error injection and error reporting module for SRAM validation.

@details
The EMU module provides hardware support for validating ECC-protected SRAM
paths. It can inject test errors into configured SRAM words, report the
address and syndrome of observed ECC events, and expose interrupt status for
single-bit correction and double-bit detection scenarios.

@section emu_features Key Features
- Per-channel SRAM error injection using a programmable target address.
- Supports data-bit injection, check-bit injection, and mixed data + check
  injection through `emu_config_t`.
- Supports raw multi-bit injection masks through EMU_DRV_InjectError().
- Provides latched error report address, error counter, and syndrome access.
- Exposes single-bit correction interrupt status and double-bit interrupt
  enable / clear helpers.
- Adapts to device-specific channel counts through `EMU_EICHD_COUNT` and
  `EMU_ERINFO_COUNT`.
- Supports 64-bit data injection masks on devices that define
  `FEATURE_EMU_SUPPORT_64BIT_INJECTION`.

@section emu_modes Supported Modes

The EMU module supports the following injection and reporting modes:

| Mode | Configuration Path | Description | Notes |
|------|--------------------|-------------|-------|
| Single data-bit injection | `injectBitsType = EMU_INJECT_BITS_TYPE_DATA` and `dataBit = EMU_DATABIT_n` | Injects one ECC test error on the SRAM data path. | Typical flow for validating single-bit correction behavior. |
| Single check-bit injection | `injectBitsType = EMU_INJECT_BITS_TYPE_CHK` and `chkBit = EMU_CHKBIT_n` | Injects one ECC test error on the ECC check-bit path. | Useful for verifying syndrome and report handling. |
| Mixed single-bit injection | `injectBitsType = EMU_INJECT_BITS_TYPE_MIXTURE` with both `dataBit` and `chkBit` | Injects one data-bit error together with one check-bit error. | Lets the application exercise combined fault scenarios. |
| Raw multi-bit injection | EMU_DRV_InjectError() with `dataMulti` and `chkMulti` masks | Programs multi-bit data and/or check masks directly. | Pass `NO_INJECTION_ERROR` for the path that should remain unchanged. |
| Interrupt-assisted error handling | `interruptEnable` in `emu_config_t` plus interrupt APIs | Latches single-bit correction status and supports double-bit interrupt control. | Signal-bit and double-bit interrupt enables are both configured during EMU_DRV_Init(). |

@section emu_arch Module Architecture

The EMU module is organized in a two-layer architecture:

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Application Code                │
│         (calls EMU_DRV_* functions)          │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          EMU Driver Layer (emu_driver.h/c)   │
│  ● Instance-based API (EMU_DRV_Init, etc.)   │
│  ● Converts user configuration into channel  │
│    injection, report, and interrupt setup    │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│      EMU HW Access Layer (emu_hw_access.h/c) │
│  ● Direct register-level helpers for EIGCR,  │
│    EICHCR, EICHD, ERINFO, ERIE, and ERIF     │
│  ● Encapsulates reset, enable, injection,    │
│    report, and interrupt register updates    │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│           EMU Peripheral Hardware            │
│      (SRAM ECC injection and reporting)      │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection emu_arch_driver Driver Layer (emu_driver.h)
Application code should use the `EMU_DRV_*` functions from emu_driver.h.
These APIs accept a zero-based instance index, validate basic constraints,
and resolve the peripheral base address internally through `EMU_BASE_PTRS`.

@subsection emu_arch_hw HW Access Layer (emu_hw_access.h)
This internal layer provides register-level helpers grouped into five
functional areas:
- **Initialization** - EMU_Init()
- **Module Enable Control** - EMU_Enable(), EMU_Disable()
- **Injection Configuration** - EMU_SetErrInjectAddr(), EMU_SetErrInjectData(),
  EMU_SetErrInjectChkbit(), and related clear / multi-bit helpers
- **Error Reporting** - EMU_GetErrReportCnt(), EMU_ClearErrReportCnt(),
  EMU_GetErrReportAddr(), EMU_GetSyndrome()
- **Interrupt Control** - EMU_EnableInterruptSignalBit(),
  EMU_EnableInterruptDoubleBit(), and corresponding clear / query helpers

@section emu_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection emu_config_inject emu_inject_err_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default Value |
|-------|------|-------------|---------------|
| injectBitsType | emu_inject_bits_type | Selects whether injection targets the data path, the check-bit path, or both. | User-defined |
| dataBit | e_emu_databit | Data-bit index used when `injectBitsType` includes the data path. | User-defined |
| chkBit | e_emu_chkbit | Check-bit index used when `injectBitsType` includes the check-bit path. | User-defined |

@subsection emu_config_struct emu_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default Value |
|-------|------|-------------|---------------|
| channel | uint32_t | Target EMU channel index. Valid range is `0 .. EMU_EICHD_COUNT - 1`. | User-defined |
| injectErrAddr | uint32_t | SRAM word address monitored for injected ECC errors. | User-defined |
| injectErrSetInfo | emu_inject_err_t | Single-bit or mixed-bit injection selection. | User-defined |
| interruptEnable | bool | Enables both signal-bit and double-bit interrupts during initialization when set to `true`. | User-defined |

@subsection emu_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| EMU_INSTANCE_COUNT | Number of EMU peripheral instances available on the device. |
| EMU_EICHD_COUNT | Number of injection channels supported by one EMU instance. |
| EMU_ERINFO_COUNT | Number of error-report entries exposed by one EMU instance. |
| FEATURE_EMU_SUPPORT_64BIT_INJECTION | Defined as `1` when data-path injection supports 64-bit masks. |
| FEATURE_EMU_GLOBAL_ENABLE_KEY | Defined as `1` when the global enable register requires a device-specific key sequence. |

@section emu_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection emu_usage_basic Pattern 1: Single-Bit Data Injection and Address Reporting
Configure one channel for data-bit injection, enable it immediately, read the
target word, and then retrieve the latched error address.

@code{.c}
#define INST_EMU      (0U)
#define TEST_WORD_ADDR (0x1FFF0000U)

void emu_single_bit_example(void)
{
    emu_config_t emuConfig = {
        .channel = 0U,
        .injectErrAddr = TEST_WORD_ADDR,
        .injectErrSetInfo = {
            .injectBitsType = EMU_INJECT_BITS_TYPE_DATA,
            .dataBit = EMU_DATABIT_7,
            .chkBit = EMU_CHKBIT_0 /* Ignored in data-only mode. */
        },
        .interruptEnable = true
    };
    volatile uint32_t *const testWord = (volatile uint32_t *)TEST_WORD_ADDR;
    uint32_t correctedValue;
    uint32_t reportAddr;

    *testWord = 0x0000BEEFU;

    /* Clock setup is platform-specific and must be completed beforehand. */
    EMU_DRV_Init(INST_EMU, &emuConfig, 1U);

    /* Reading the configured address triggers the injected ECC test event. */
    correctedValue = *testWord;
    reportAddr = EMU_DRV_GetErrReportAddr(INST_EMU, (uint8_t)emuConfig.channel);

    (void)correctedValue;
    (void)reportAddr;

    EMU_DRV_DeInit(INST_EMU, emuConfig.channel);
}
@endcode

@subsection emu_usage_multi Pattern 2: Raw Multi-Bit Injection Masks
Use the raw multi-bit helper when the application needs to program data and
check masks directly instead of selecting one enumerated bit.

@code{.c}
#define INST_EMU       (0U)
#define TEST_WORD_ADDR (0x1FFF0000U)

void emu_multi_bit_example(void)
{
    emu_databit_type dataMask = (emu_databit_type)(((uint32_t)1U << 0U) |
                                                   ((uint32_t)1U << 3U));
    emu_chkbit_type chkMask = (emu_chkbit_type)((uint32_t)1U << 1U);

    EMU_DRV_InjectError(INST_EMU,
                        0U,
                        TEST_WORD_ADDR,
                        dataMask,
                        chkMask);

    /* To skip one path, pass NO_INJECTION_ERROR for dataMask or chkMask. */
}
@endcode

@subsection emu_usage_interrupt Pattern 3: Interrupt Service and Error Counter Maintenance
Check the single-bit correction flag in the interrupt handler, clear the
latched status, and consume the report information before clearing the count.

@code{.c}
#define INST_EMU (0U)

void EMU_SB_IRQHandler(void)
{
    if (EMU_DRV_GetChannelSBInterruptFlag(INST_EMU, 0U) != 0U)
    {
        uint8_t chkBit = EMU_DRV_GetErrReportChkbit(INST_EMU, 0U);
        uint32_t errAddr = EMU_DRV_GetErrReportAddr(INST_EMU, 0U);

        EMU_DRV_ClearInterruptFlagSignalBit(INST_EMU, 0U);
        EMU_DRV_ClearErrReportCnt(INST_EMU, 0U);

        (void)chkBit;
        (void)errAddr;
    }
}

void emu_double_bit_interrupt_control(void)
{
    EMU_DRV_EnableInterruptDoubleBit(INST_EMU, 0U);
    /* ... handle the fault path ... */
    EMU_DRV_ClearInterruptFlagDoubleBit(INST_EMU, 0U);
    EMU_DRV_DisableInterruptDoubleBit(INST_EMU, 0U);
}
@endcode

@section emu_api API Quick Reference

@subsection emu_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| EMU_DRV_Init() | Reset one EMU instance, apply the caller configuration, and optionally enable the selected channel immediately. |
| EMU_DRV_DeInit() | Disable the selected channel and restore the entire EMU instance to reset state. |

@subsection emu_api_inject Error Injection Control
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| EMU_DRV_InjectError() | Program raw multi-bit data and check masks for one channel and re-enable injection. |

@subsection emu_api_report Error Report & Counter Access
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| EMU_DRV_GetErrReportChkbit() | Convert the latched syndrome into a reported check-bit index. |
| EMU_DRV_GetErrReportCnt() | Read the per-channel error report counter. |
| EMU_DRV_ClearErrReportCnt() | Clear the per-channel error report counter. |
| EMU_DRV_GetErrReportAddr() | Read the address latched for the reported ECC event. |

@subsection emu_api_interrupt Interrupt Status & Control
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| EMU_DRV_GetChannelSBInterruptFlag() | Query whether a single-bit correction interrupt is pending for the selected channel. |
| EMU_DRV_ClearInterruptFlagSignalBit() | Clear the single-bit correction interrupt flag for one channel. |
| EMU_DRV_EnableInterruptDoubleBit() | Enable double-bit interrupt signaling for one channel. |
| EMU_DRV_DisableInterruptDoubleBit() | Disable double-bit interrupt signaling for one channel. |
| EMU_DRV_ClearInterruptFlagDoubleBit() | Clear the double-bit interrupt flag for one channel. |

@section emu_notes Important Notes

@subsection emu_notes_clock Clock Dependency
The EMU peripheral clock must be enabled before calling EMU_DRV_Init().
The driver does not manage clocks internally. See @ref clock_manager.

@subsection emu_notes_access Access Restrictions
@warning EMU error injection is intended for supervisor-mode SRAM accesses.
Using user-mode accesses may bypass the intended validation path or fail to
trigger the expected ECC event.

@warning The injection target must be accessed with 32-bit word reads and
writes. Sub-word accesses are not the supported validation path for this
driver and can produce unexpected report behavior.

@subsection emu_notes_reset Instance-Wide Reset Behavior
@warning EMU_DRV_Init() calls EMU_Init(), which resets the complete EMU
instance before applying the caller-provided configuration. Re-initializing
one channel clears the configuration and report state of the other channels
within the same instance.

@subsection emu_notes_device Device Variations
- The valid channel range is device-dependent and exposed through
  `EMU_EICHD_COUNT`.
- The number of report entries is device-dependent and exposed through
  `EMU_ERINFO_COUNT`.
- 64-bit data injection masks are only available when
  `FEATURE_EMU_SUPPORT_64BIT_INJECTION == 1`.

@subsection emu_notes_enable Global Enable Handling
When `FEATURE_EMU_GLOBAL_ENABLE_KEY == 1`, the hardware requires a specific
global-enable write value. The internal EMU_Enable() helper applies the
correct sequence automatically.

@section emu_integration Integration Guide

@subsection emu_integration_files Compile Files
The following files must be added to the project:

@code{.sh}
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/emu/emu_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/emu/emu_hw_access.c
@endcode

@subsection emu_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directories to the toolchain include search path:

@code{.sh}
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/emu
@endcode

@subsection emu_integration_symbols Preprocessor Symbols
No user-defined preprocessor symbols are required for this component. Device
capabilities are selected automatically through the active device feature
headers.

@subsection emu_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager
*/
